; ---- Gallery: which images are in the rotation ----
; The pool is built from disk (YURI_AV\selfie*.*) merged with the embedded
; images above, and every consumer of the gallery - the gate hero, the
; update-log card and the minimised pill - reads that one pool. Making the
; gallery editable therefore means editing the pool, not each of the three.
;
; Removal is a HIDE LIST, not a delete. These are the user's own photographs;
; a one-click control that erased one off disk would be the wrong control to
; put on a settings page. An exclusion list is reversible, survives a restart,
; and works identically for the embedded images, which cannot be deleted at
; all because they live inside the script.
