; Stored as lowercase filenames joined with "|" - a stable key across launches
; in the way a pool index is not (see SelKey).
; ---- iniPath is assigned HERE, not 30 lines below ----
; It used to be declared further down, past this point, and a top-level
; `global x := v` is two separate things: the declaration is hoisted, but the
; assignment is an ordinary statement that only runs when control flow reaches
; it. So the read below ran against an UNSET variable, IniRead threw, the `try`
; swallowed it, and galHide came back "" on every single launch.
