; ---- re-apply (holding) state ----
; Roblox does not overwrite flags at a steady trickle - it rewrites them in a
; burst, at the moment the flag table is rebuilt for a new place or server.
; A fixed poll is the wrong shape for that: slow enough to be cheap while
; nothing is happening is also slow enough to lose the only window that
; matters. So the tick rate follows what is actually going on.
FFM.raBurst  := 0          ; ticks left at the fast rate
FFM.raKey    := ""         ; table identity the drift counters belong to
FFM.raDrift  := Map()      ; flag name -> times it has been put back
FFM.raStuck  := Map()      ; flag name -> consecutive writes that did not take
; ---- unwritable flags: back off instead of grinding ----
; A flag whose write never takes - a page that discards writes, a stale value
; pointer, or Roblox rewriting it faster than we can - was retried on EVERY
; tick forever. At the burst rate that is three futile write-plus-readback
; cycles a second, per flag, indefinitely. These two hold a per-flag skip
; countdown so a provably unwritable flag costs almost nothing while a flag
; that recovers is picked straight back up.
FFM.raSkip   := Map()      ; flag name -> ticks still to skip
FFM.raSkipN  := Map()      ; flag name -> current backoff length
