; ---- what QUIET MODE is allowed to touch ----
; An allowlist, never a heuristic. Deciding at runtime that something "looks
; idle" and demoting it is how a user ends up with a stuttering call and no way
; to connect it to this switch.
;
; Deliberately absent: Discord, Spotify, OBS, any capture or audio tool. They
; are exactly the processes that are cheap on average and catastrophic to
; starve for the one millisecond that matters, and BELOW_NORMAL only ever bites
; under contention - which is precisely when their audio thread misses.
; Browsers are in because a browser with hardware acceleration and thirty tabs
; is, on most machines, the single largest thing Roblox is competing with.
;
; ---- and three that were removed after they were added ----
; SearchApp.exe is the Start menu and search UI. Demoting it costs nothing
; while the game has focus and then makes Start feel sluggish the moment you
; alt-tab out - a degradation the user WILL notice, bought for a saving they
; will not. The indexer behind it (SearchIndexer) is the part that actually
; burns CPU and it stays.
; backgroundTaskHost.exe hosts arbitrary UWP background work, which is another
; way of saying nobody here knows what is inside it.
; CompPkgSrv.exe is idle almost all of the time, so demoting it buys nothing
; and is one more process touched for no reason.
