; ---- the machine-wide registry set ----
; Every entry is a documented Windows value, and every entry is journalled to
; disk BEFORE it is written - see SPFFpsJnl*. `adm` marks the ones under HKLM,
; which are skipped rather than attempted when YURI is not elevated: a write
; that throws would leave the row claiming a setting it never made.
;
; What is deliberately NOT in here, having been considered and rejected:
;   Win32PrioritySeparation - the encoding of the value everybody recommends is
;     contradicted by half the sources that recommend it, and writing a number
;     into the scheduler's quantum control that cannot be explained is not a
;     tweak, it is a guess with a reboot attached.
;   HwSchMode (hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling) - genuinely a coin flip by
;     GPU and driver, and it needs a reboot to take either way. Read and
;     reported by SPFHags, never written.
;   Fullscreen-optimisation overrides - as likely to lose the flip-model
;     present path as to win the exclusive one.
;   HPET / bcdedit / disabling services - out of proportion to what is being
;     bought, and the failure modes reach well past a frame rate.
; `dir` is which way is BETTER for that value: -1 lower, +1 higher, 0 exact.
; It is what stops this feature undoing somebody else's tuning. SystemResponsiveness
; is the one that made it necessary - lower is better there, the default is 20,
; and a user who has already taken it to 0 would have been RAISED to our 10 by
; a switch sold as making things faster.
global SPF_FPS_REG := [
    {k: "gamedvr", key: "HKCU\System\GameConfigStore", v: "GameDVR_Enabled"
     , t: "REG_DWORD", want: 0, dir: -1, adm: 0
     , n: "game dvr"}
  , {k: "appcap", key: "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\GameDVR"
     , v: "AppCaptureEnabled", t: "REG_DWORD", want: 0, dir: -1, adm: 0
