; ---- row 6 carries chips too, and narrower ones ----
; Row 1's chips REPLACE its hint, because once DISCORD ACTIVITY is on the hint
; has nothing left to say. Row 6's hint is the opposite: the client count, the
; lever tally and the bottleneck reading are the only proof this switch does
; anything, so the chips take the left of the line and the hint slides right
; into what is left rather than fading out under them. Two chips at 74 leave
; the hint about 140px, which elides cleanly.
; Three at 66, not two at 74: tw on this panel is 276px and the hint still has
; to fit beside them. See SPFFpsHintShort - what is left is deliberately terse,
; and the long form goes to the status line where there is room for it.
; ---- and their OWN zone band ----
; 984 + k was a collision, not a base: 980 + i is the row switch band, so 985
; was MULTI-ROBLOX INSTANCES' switch and 986 was FPS BOOST's own. Clicking the
; GPU chip toggled multi-instance because that is genuinely whose zone it was.
