; ================= the gate moved ================
; It used to stand here, before anything was loaded, and it asked for a key.
; It asks for nothing now and it stands AFTER the loading screen - see
; LaunchGate, called just before the hub opens - so that opening the .ahk
; starts the load at once and the first thing anybody decides is where to
; start: Roblox and the hub, or the hub alone. The key machinery (KeyFetch*,
; KeyOk, the keyfetch child) is left in place and idle.

; ================= window (autoblock overlay: created dormant, shown by the hub) =================
; Created BEFORE the loading screen, not after. Every background lookup the
; loader depends on posts its answer back by WM_COPYDATA, and the child is told
; which window to post to - so with no window and no handler there was nothing
; to receive a reply and nothing to send one to. SPFStatsFetch even opens with
; `if (id = "" || !IsSet(ui)) return`, which meant the loader's
; SPFPrefetchTick() call returned without doing anything at all: the screen
; showed "resolving saved places [N]" while resolving none of them, and every
; entry arrived in the hub still saying "loading game details...".
; The window is created hidden and the input handlers stay below, so nothing
; becomes interactive early - only the message plumbing moves up.
; AlwaysOnTop is folded in rather than fixed: the flag is read from zeal.ini a
; few lines above, so a window created here already honours the setting instead
; of being created topmost and demoted a frame later.
global ui := Gui("-Caption +E0x80000 +E0x8000000 " (hubTop ? "+AlwaysOnTop " : "") "+ToolWindow -DPIScale", "YURIOVERLAY")
ui.Show("NA x0 y0 w" PW " h" PH)
ui.Hide()
