; CopyData dispatches on the magic value alone, not on which window received
; it, so registering it here serves the loader and the hub equally.
OnMessage(0x4A, CopyData)
; WM_DISPLAYCHANGE is a HINT that the metrics are worth re-reading, not proof
; that they moved. Windows broadcasts it for any mode set - including a client
; entering and leaving exclusive fullscreen at the desktop's own resolution -
; so it goes through DisplayNudge, which asks ScreenMoved the same question the
; 1 Hz watcher asks and reacts only if the answer is yes.
OnMessage(0x7E, DisplayNudge)         ; WM_DISPLAYCHANGE: look, then decide
SetTimer(ScreenWatch, 1000)           ; ... and do not trust the message to arrive

