; !PZ_cal: this variant has no ~, so it CONSUMES the click. With AUTOBLOCK
; armed and Roblox focused that swallows the very corner clicks grid setup is
; asking for, and neither the game nor PUZZLE AI ever sees them. The two cannot
; sensibly be doing their jobs at the same moment, so blocking stands down for
; the few seconds setup is running.
;
; !PZ_solving is the same argument for the same reason, and it was missing. The
; solve drives the mouse itself, so every line it draws presented this hotkey
; with a left press over the board while Roblox was focused - all four
; conditions true - and the press was consumed rather than delivered. The stamp
; on PZ_SelfMark now stops those events reaching the hook at all; this guard is
; the one that does not depend on an undocumented constant still being right.
;
; The RELEASE context below is deliberately NOT guarded. It carries ~, so it
; blocks nothing, and its only job is making sure a q that went down comes back
; up - a safety valve that should stay open even while a solve runs.
#HotIf enabled && !PZ_cal && !PZ_solving && WinActive("ahk_exe RobloxPlayerBeta.exe") && !HitZoneAtCursor()
*LButton:: {
    SendInput "{Blind}{q down}"
    global lastClick := A_TickCount
    global qCount
    qCount += 1
}
