    ; It was routed through the release path (`wasClick && z = 205`) instead,
    ; and that can never fire: wasClick is HL.drag = 1, which only the window
    ; drag zone ever sets, and HL.dragZone is never set for a plain button. The
    ; button rendered, lit on hover, popped on press - and did nothing.
    if (z = 205) {
